{
  "kicker": "NanoColloids & Magnetism Lab",
  "title": "Our group focuses on designing and synthesizing nanomaterials with controlled shapes and properties, exploring structures such as clusters, nanosheets, and elongated assemblies, and investigating applications including magnetic hyperthermia.",
  "intro": "<p>We exploit the surface chemistry and magnetism of nanomaterials to control their colloidal stability and assembly behavior. We investigate magnetization and magnetic heat losses of magnetic nanoparticles dispersed in different media under alternating magnetic fields.</p>\n<p>This website showcases the research developed within the framework of the Ramón y Cajal project, which focuses on creating scalable, high-performance magnetic nanostructures for biomedical applications. It has been funded by the Spanish Ministry of Science and Innovation through the Ramón y Cajal 2021 program (RYC2021‐032448‐I).</p>",
